::CW_U04_L05_Q01::Line: The garden gave off a fragrance after rain. Which connotation is strongest?{
~A. Harsh and rotten.#Incorrect. Fragrance is usually pleasant.
=
~C. Neutral and mechanical.#Incorrect. Fragrance is not mechanical.
~D. Angry and loud.#Incorrect. The word describes scent, not anger or sound.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q02::Line: The garden gave off a stench after rain. What style does stench create?{
~B. Gentle and graceful.#Incorrect. Stench does not support gentleness.
~C. Formal and respectful.#Incorrect. Stench is not formal praise.
~D. Bright and musical.#Incorrect. It refers to smell, not sound.
=
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q03::Line: The slim road curved through the valley. Which word has a similar denotation but a more negative connotation than slim?{
=
~A. narrow.#Incorrect. Narrow is mostly neutral.
~B. winding.#Incorrect. Winding describes shape, not thinness negatively.
~D. graceful.#Incorrect. Graceful is positive, not negative.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q04::Line: The child clutched the tattered blanket. What does tattered add?{
~A. A sense that the blanket is new.#Incorrect. Tattered means worn or torn.
~B. A cheerful party style.#Incorrect. The word suggests wear, not celebration.
=
~C. No connotation at all.#Incorrect. Tattered carries a worn, possibly sad feeling.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q05::Line: The lake was quiet. Which revision creates the most peaceful style?{
=
~B. The lake snarled under the dock.#Incorrect. Snarled creates threat.
~C. The lake choked on weeds.#Incorrect. Choked is negative.
~D. The lake cracked its teeth.#Incorrect. This is harsh and uneasy.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q06::Line: The hallway was filled with noise. Which word choice creates the harshest style?{
~A. music.#Incorrect. Music can be pleasant.
~C. murmur.#Incorrect. Murmur suggests softness.
~D. hush.#Incorrect. Hush suggests quiet.
=
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q07::Line: The stranger smiled. Which revision gives smile a suspicious connotation?{
~A. The stranger grinned warmly.#Incorrect. Warmly is positive.
=
~B. The stranger smiled kindly.#Incorrect. Kindly is positive.
~D. The stranger beamed with joy.#Incorrect. Beamed with joy is positive.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q08::Line: The house stood at the end of the road. Which diction creates a lonely style?{
~B. The house sparkled with music.#Incorrect. This creates a lively style.
~C. The house danced with color.#Incorrect. This creates energy.
=
~D. The house cheered at the road.#Incorrect. This is joyful, not lonely.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q09::Line: The old coat hung by the door. Which word gives old a more affectionate connotation?{
~A. ragged.#Incorrect. Ragged is negative.
~B. ancient.#Incorrect. Ancient can be formal or distant.
~D. ruined.#Incorrect. Ruined is strongly negative.
=
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q10::Line: The wind moved through the grass. Which revision creates an uneasy style?{
=
~B. The wind hummed through the grass.#Incorrect. Hummed is softer.
~C. The wind drifted through the grass.#Incorrect. Drifted is calm.
~D. The wind rested in the grass.#Incorrect. Rested is peaceful.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q11::Line: Her room was small. Which word choice makes small feel cozy rather than cramped?{
~A. cramped.#Incorrect. Cramped feels uncomfortable.
~C. airless.#Incorrect. Airless is negative.
=
~D. boxed-in.#Incorrect. Boxed-in suggests restriction.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q12::Line: The path went into the trees. Which diction creates a mysterious style?{
~B. The path continued into the trees.#Incorrect. Continued is neutral.
=
~C. The path was measured into the trees.#Incorrect. Measured is awkward and not mysterious.
~D. The path explained the trees.#Incorrect. This does not fit the meaning.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q13::Line: The candle gave light. Which revision creates the gentlest style?{
=
~A. The candle glared against the wall.#Incorrect. Glared is harsh.
~B. The candle burned the wall.#Incorrect. Burned is destructive.
~D. The candle attacked the wall.#Incorrect. Attacked is violent.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q14::Line: He walked into the room. Which verb creates the most confident style?{
~B. crept.#Incorrect. Crept suggests caution.
~C. shuffled.#Incorrect. Shuffled suggests uncertainty or tiredness.
~D. stumbled.#Incorrect. Stumbled suggests awkwardness.
=
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q15::Line: The speaker used the word childish. What connotation does childish usually carry?{
~A. Positive innocence.#Incorrect. Childlike is more often positive.
~C. Neutral age only.#Incorrect. It carries judgment.
=
~D. Formal respect.#Incorrect. It is not respectful diction.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q16::Line: The speaker used the word childlike. What connotation does childlike usually carry?{
~B. Annoying and immature.#Incorrect. Childish would better fit that.
=
~C. Harsh and cruel.#Incorrect. Childlike does not suggest cruelty.
~D. Mechanical and cold.#Incorrect. It relates to human qualities.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q17::Line: The water was clear. Which revision creates a formal, elevated style?{
~A. The water was okay.#Incorrect. Okay is informal.
~C. The water was kind of shiny.#Incorrect. Kind of is informal.
~D. The water was stuff.#Incorrect. Stuff is vague.
=
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q18::Line: The abandoned store stared with boarded eyes. Which style is created by abandoned and boarded?{
=
~B. Festive and crowded.#Incorrect. The diction suggests the opposite.
~C. Playful and silly.#Incorrect. The image is unsettling.
~D. Calm and polished.#Incorrect. Boarded and abandoned feel rough.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q19::Line: The final note floated into the rafters. What connotation does floated carry?{
~A. Heavy and violent.#Incorrect. Floated is light.
=
~C. Angry and sharp.#Incorrect. It is not angry diction.
~D. Rotten and unpleasant.#Incorrect. It does not suggest decay.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q20::Line: The city lights glittered in the rain. Which word creates a bright style?{
~B. sulked.#Incorrect. Sulked suggests moodiness.
~C. decayed.#Incorrect. Decayed suggests rot.
=
~D. limped.#Incorrect. Limped suggests weakness.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q21::Line: The apology hovered between us. Which connotation does hovered add?{
=
~A. Resolved and finished.#Incorrect. Hovered suggests unresolved suspension.
~C. Loud and joyful.#Incorrect. It does not suggest loudness.
~D. Ancient and formal.#Incorrect. It does not primarily suggest age.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q22::Line: The porch sagged under the heat. Which style is created by sagged?{
~B. Bright and playful.#Incorrect. Sagged is not playful.
~C. Clean and polished.#Incorrect. The word suggests strain.
=
~D. Fast and excited.#Incorrect. Sagged is slow and heavy.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q23::Line: The road stretched ahead. Which revision adds a hopeful style?{
~A. The road threatened ahead.#Incorrect. Threatened creates fear.
~C. The road collapsed ahead.#Incorrect. Collapsed is negative.
~D. The road vanished behind us.#Incorrect. Vanished can suggest uncertainty or loss.
=
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q24::Line: The rain tapped the roof. Which word has a harsher connotation than tapped?{
~B. touched.#Incorrect. Touched is gentle.
=
~C. brushed.#Incorrect. Brushed is light.
~D. whispered.#Incorrect. Whispered is soft.
}

::CW_U04_L05_Q25::Line: The speaker chooses crisp instead of cold to describe morning air. What effect does crisp create?{
=
~B. It suggests rotten smell.#Incorrect. Crisp does not suggest rot.
~C. It removes all style.#Incorrect. The word shapes style.
~D. It means the air is hot.#Incorrect. Crisp air is cool.
}
